      say: `This is the one place the code deliberately overrides the program's own setting, and it ties straight back to Chapter 2. The emergency accounts hold Global Administrator permanently. A monthly review of that role, set to remove access on silence with auto-apply on, would quietly remove them the first month reviewers miss. Learn itself warns that the combination can revoke all access. So that one series makes no change on silence, and anything left unreviewed turns into an evidence finding instead. Every other series still removes access when reviewers stay silent.`,
      detail: `PA-AR-06 is the one guard that changes the program's setting. The emergency accounts hold Global Administrator as permanent active assignments (Chapter 02). A review of Global Administrator that covers active assignments, with "remove access" on silence and auto-apply on, removes them if the reviewers miss one month. So a review that covers the emergency accounts' permanent Global Administrator uses "no change" on silence, and an unreviewed item becomes an evidence finding instead (PA-AR-E04). Every other privileged series removes access on silence. That is the owner's decision (research gaps, row 74), and Book 04, Chapter 08's Step 8 records the exception. The Graph settings page: auto-apply defaults to false; the default decision can be Approve, Deny or Recommendation; and it cautions that both together can revoke all access.`,
