      say: `Lab 1 runs on a laptop with no tenant. First, run Learn's tutorial against the fake. Eleven tests pass, and the third one shows the trap: send the tutorial's request twice, and you get two reviews with the same name. Next, list each task's permissions: reads for planning and evidence, writes only for the apply. Then the dry run. It finds one series to create, two to update, one to replace, three already right, and one somebody made by hand in the portal. Nothing is sent. Only two writes would go out, because the Azure update needs the preview switch.`,
      detail: `You need PowerShell 7.1 or later with Pester 5. Work in examples/privileged-access. Step 1, run Learn's tutorial against the fake: Invoke-Pester -Path tests/AccessReviews.Tests.ps1 -FullNameFilter '*(Learn), run as published*' -Output None -PassThru | Select-Object PassedCount, FailedCount gives PassedCount 11, FailedCount 0. Read the third test: the tutorial's POST, sent twice, leaves two series with the same name. Step 2, list each task's permissions: Import-Module ./powershell/PaAccessReviews/PaAccessReviews.psm1, then Get-PaArRequiredPermission for access-reviews-plan, access-reviews-apply and access-reviews-evidence: AccessReview.Read.All and Reader for the plan and the evidence; AccessReview.ReadWrite.All and User Access Administrator for apply. Step 3, run the dry run: ./Invoke-PaAccessReviews.ps1 -Cloud gcc -Mode Plan -ConfigPath tests/fixtures/ch07/access-reviews.json -FixturePath tests/fixtures/ch07/tenant.json -AsOf 2026-10-30 -OutputPath out/reviews-plan. Output: "Plan: 1 Create, 2 Update, 1 Replace, 3 NoChange, 1 Unmanaged"; "Checks: 0 Finding, 1 Warn, 1 Info"; "Dry run: nothing sent (2 write(s) would be sent with -Apply)"; "Written to out/reviews-plan (manifest.json lists every request and file hash)". Step 4, read the diff: Get-Content out/reviews-plan/plan.json -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json | Format-Table name, action, changes. Global Administrator and the Azure Owner series: Update, settings.instanceDurationInDays (the tenant has 7 days, the JSON 14). Privileged Role Administrator: Create. Exchange: Replace, reviewers (an old reviewer group). The three PRV-* membership series: NoChange. PAR-T0-SecurityAdministrator-Monthly, made by hand in the portal: Unmanaged. The application review without the prefix isn't listed. The two writes the dry run counts are the Graph ones; the Azure update needs -IncludePreview. bodies/ holds each request body for review. The commands run Learn's pinned requests and the example against a fictional tenant served by a fake. They show what the code does, not that Graph or Resource Manager return the same shapes.`,
