      say: `The second half of the lab is where it gets convincing. Run the example's checks on Learn's own request body, and it fails on the fallback reviewer, the missing instructions and auto-apply. Apply in the fake, and only the two planned writes go out; everything else is skipped with a reason. Read the evidence, and every kind of problem turns up, from an overdue review to an emergency account that was denied. Then try to switch the Global Administrator series to deny on silence: the apply refuses, and nothing is sent.`,
      detail: `Step 5, check Learn's body with the example's rules: . ./tests/AccessReviewsSampleHarness.ps1; Test-PaArDefinition -Body (Get-ArTutorialCreateRequest).Body -AsOf 2026-10-30 | Format-Table Rule, Severity gives PA-AR-02, PA-AR-03 and PA-AR-05 as Findings, PA-AR-07 and PA-AR-10 as Warns. Step 6, apply in the fake: the dry-run command with -OutputPath out/reviews-apply -Apply, then results.json as Name, Action, Result, Note. "Applied: 2 write(s) sent; Replace and Unmanaged series are left for a person". Global Administrator and Privileged Role Administrator are Sent, read back; Exchange, the three PRV-* series, the Azure series and the unmanaged one are Skipped, each with its reason. The fake starts from the fixture on every run, so nothing carries over to the next step. Step 7, read the evidence: ./Invoke-PaAccessReviews.ps1 -Cloud gcc -Mode Evidence ... -OutputPath out/reviews-evidence, then findings.json as Rule, Severity, Object. "Evidence: 18 decisions in 7 instances; 7 Finding, 2 Warn". PA-AR-E01 for Privileged Role Administrator (not in this tenant yet), PA-AR-E02 for PRV-T0-GlobalAdmin (its last review ended September 15), PA-AR-E08 for Emergency Access 02 (denied in October), PA-AR-E04 for Frank Ode (unreviewed, Tier 0) and as a Warn for Gina Lee (Tier 1), PA-AR-E05 for Carl Ops, PA-AR-E03 for Frank Ode's Exchange denial that didn't apply, PA-AR-E06 for Bo Chen, who approved their own access, and PA-AR-E07 for one Exchange reviewer's five approvals in two minutes. Step 8, see the lockout guard: read the config, set defaultDecision to 'Deny' on PAR-T0-GlobalAdministrator-Monthly, build an apply client on the fake and call Invoke-PaArApply with -Apply: "Refusing -Apply: the plan has 1 Finding(s): PA-AR-06 PAR-T0-GlobalAdministrator-Monthly". Nothing is sent. Step 9, Invoke-Pester -Path tests. Expected result: 330 tests passing, and each row of the gap table seen with your own eyes. Delete out when you're done; the evidence folder names people. The tests: this chapter's are the 57 in tests/AccessReviews.Tests.ps1: 11 on Learn's tutorial as published, then the calls and permissions, the reviewed JSON and bodies, each rule, the plan's actions, -Apply and its refusals, the evidence and its paging, and the entry script's manifest. With Chapters 01, 02, 03 and 06, 208 Pester tests pass under PowerShell 7, with no module, tenant or network.`,
